From: northbridgeforge <northbridgeforge@pm.me>
Subject: [PATCH] virtio-gpu: include DisplayID 1.3 display parameters

A standalone DisplayID display needs a Display Parameters data block.
Insert the revision-0, 12-byte block before the existing Type I timing.
Describe the caller's virtual display in 0.1 mm units, not a host panel.
Use checked direct native pixel counts and coherent unspecified pairs
for zero or unrepresentable sizes. Normalize and round the aspect ratio,
explicitly saturating it at 3.55 (lossy for more extreme ratios); there
is no unspecified aspect sentinel. Use 1:1 only when neither ratio is
usable. Keep the Type I timing bytes and the legacy EDID path unchanged.

Applies after patch 0020 to SteaMac's libkrun v1.19.6 series. Extend the
existing tests for units, bounds, portrait ratios, rounding and fallback.
---
